   <standOff><listPerson><person xml:id="person3747"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">maitreya</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'phags pa byams pa</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">byams pa mgon po</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">maitreyanātha</persName><sex value="M"/><nationality>Indic</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P6118</idno><idno type="APIS">3747</idno><note type="comment">Future Buddha held as the author of the works that come to be designated as the "Five Jewels of Maitreya" (ID:6167).</note></person><person xml:id="person3756"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">asaṅga</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">slob dpon thogs med</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">thogs myed</persName><sex value="M"/><nationality>Indic</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P6117</idno><idno type="APIS">3756</idno></person><person xml:id="person5806"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">lha rigs 'od gsal rad Na mir+ba</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">ལྷ་རིགས་འོད་གསལ་རད་ཎ་མིརྦ</persName><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="APIS">5806</idno><note type="comment">The reading of the last syllable is unclear: mir+ba, or mar+tsi; the editors of [BA7CVGHQ] read: mati&lt;s&gt;.</note></person><person xml:id="person6026"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">tshul khrims dpal</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">ཚུལ་ཁྲིམས་དཔལ</persName><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="APIS">6026</idno><note type="comment">Maybe identical with sKyo ston (ID:4052). A Zhwa dmar Tshul khrims dpal (1096-1132) (bdr:P4426) was a student of sGam po pa (ID:4189) and Dwags sgom Tshul khrims snying po (ID:6157).</note></person></listPerson><listBibl><bibl xml:id="work5223"><title type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">chos dang chos nyid rnam par